OL,3,GNEWSA'Invincible' boy recovering after
OL,4,Abeing hit by car
OL,5,
OL,6,FA schoolboy has spoken of his
OL,7,Fcontinuing recovery from catastrophic
OL,8,Fbrain injuries he suffered when he was
OL,9,Fhit by a car.
OL,11,FCharlie was seriously hurt when he was
OL,12,Fknocked down as he walked home from
OL,13,Fschool in Braunstone, Leicester, in
OL,14,FFebruary 2025.
OL,16,FHe was taken to the Queen's Medical
OL,17,FCentre in Nottingham, where he spent
OL,18,Fweeks in a coma before beginning
OL,19,Frehabilitation. It has meant learning
OL,20,Fagain how to walk and speak, as well as
OL,21,Fdo simple things like cleaning his
OL,22,Fteeth.
OL,23,APub: 23-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
